    "description": "Gray Swan Indirect Prompt Injection Arena: a public red-teaming competition (with UK AISI, US CAISI, and labs) for concealed indirect prompt injections in tool-use, coding, and computer-use agents. Success requires both a harmful action and concealment in the user-facing reply. Cards report attacker success probability after k attempts (for example k=1, 10, 15). The open-source release ships 41 scenarios; 95 non-transferring Qwen attacks are public, while the full competition attack set is held for labs and AISI.",
